Adding a New Tool to the Catalog
================================
Everything lives in src/catalog/data.go. To add e.g. "Rust" to the
Languages category:

  1. Add translation keys to every file in i18n/locales/ (at least
     en.json, ideally all of them.):

       "item.rust.description": "Rust toolchain"

  2. Add the item to the right Category.Items slice:

       {
           ID:             "rust",
           Name:           "Rust",
           DescriptionKey: "item.rust.description",
           MacOS:          InstallCommand{Command: "brew", Args: []string{"install", "rust"}},
           Windows:        InstallCommand{Command: "winget", Args: []string{"install", "-e", "--id", "Rustlang.Rustup"}},
           Linux: map[system.PackageManager]InstallCommand{
               system.Apt:    {Command: "apt-get", Args: []string{"install", "-y", "rustc", "cargo"}},
               system.Dnf:    {Command: "dnf", Args: []string{"install", "-y", "rust", "cargo"}},
               system.Pacman: {Command: "pacman", Args: []string{"-S", "--noconfirm", "rust"}},
               system.Zypper: {Command: "zypper", Args: []string{"install", "-y", "rust", "cargo"}},
               system.Apk:    {Command: "apk", Args: []string{"add", "rust", "cargo"}},
           },
       }

  3. Leaving a platform's InstallCommand zero-valued (or a PM out of
     the Linux map) is fine as CommandFor just returns ok = false
     and the wizard prints installer.noCommand and skips it.


Adding a Whole New Category
---------------------------
Add a new Category{NameKey: "category.whatever", Items: [...]} entry
to the slice returned by catalog.All(), plus the matching
category.whatever key in the locale files. The wizard iterates
catalog.All() automatically, so nothing else needs to change.
